  "narrative": "All twelve conditional Welch comparisons are valid and have adequate cell sizes. They provide strong evidence that the three accepted marginal associations are not simply eliminated when conditioning on one other accepted predictor. feature_037=1 versus 0 remains associated with much stronger dependency in all tested feature_002 and feature_010 strata: signed estimates range from +0.809 to +0.865 and every lower bound exceeds +0.64. feature_002=1 versus 0 remains associated with much weaker dependency in all tested feature_037 and feature_010 strata: signed estimates range from +0.780 to +0.990 with lower bounds above +0.71. feature_010=1 versus 0 remains associated with weaker dependency across all tested feature_037 and feature_002 strata: signed estimates range from +0.367 to +0.576 with lower bounds from +0.206 to +0.414, still above the 0.15-unit meaningful-effect threshold. I therefore accept H37 through H48. These results make a simple single-proxy interpretation less likely, because attenuation of one predictor by one other accepted predictor is small relative to the observed effects. However, they are stratified conditional contrasts, not simultaneous adjusted models, and they remain dataset-specific associations. There are suggestive differences: feature_002 may be larger in the feature_010=1 stratum, and feature_010 may be larger in the feature_002=1 stratum, although overlapping intervals mean formal interactions are needed. Multiplicity across twelve comparisons is a concern for borderline threshold claims, but here the effects are large and coherent across predictor-specific strata; H46 and H47 are the most uncertain feature_010 conditional estimates. I request validation of H21 because feature_010 is the weakest of the three accepted full-cohort claims; independent evidence will help determine whether to maintain the feature_010 claims as stable dataset-specific associations or treat them as discovery-specific findings. These results do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability beyond this supplied dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 3 appraise: H37-H48 accepted and active. Mutual single-stratum conditioning does not materially attenuate the large feature_037/feature_002 associations and moderately supports feature_010. Possible interactions: feature_002 stronger when feature_010=1; feature_010 stronger when feature_002=1. Next priorities: analyze registered pairwise interactions H49-H54 and double-stratum claims H55-H60 if cell sizes allow. Validation requested for H21. If H21 validation is null or below threshold, reassess all feature_010 claims including H21, H45-H48 as discovery-specific rather than stable. If H21 validates, the accepted predictor set H16/H19/H21 plus conditional refinements becomes stronger dataset-specific evidence, still noncausal. H25-H36 remain lower-priority broad continuous/categorical screening. Avoid interpreting stratified contrasts as adjusted causal effects; residual confounding and correlated latent groups remain possible."
